<p>San Marcos Public Adjuster serves San Marcos, the rest of Hays County, and neighboring communities in Caldwell, Comal, and Guadalupe counties. We do not run storefront offices. Instead, we come to the damaged property, inspect it, document the loss, and handle the claim with your insurer from there. Below is a look at each area we cover and the kinds of weather it has actually recorded, drawn from the NOAA National Centers for Environmental Information (NCEI) Storm Events Database and National Weather Service summaries.</p>
<p>To check reports near a specific place, search a city or ZIP code with the <a href="/storm-lookup/">storm lookup tool</a> or browse <a href="/storm-history/">Hays County storm history</a>.</p>

<h2>San Marcos: our home service area</h2>
<p>San Marcos is the Hays County seat, sitting on I-35 about 25 miles south of Austin, with Texas State University and the spring-fed San Marcos River at its center. The Census Bureau’s Vintage 2025 estimate puts the population at 77,830. As a <a href="/">San Marcos public adjuster</a>, most of our work starts here, and the NOAA record shows why. Hays County has logged 180 hail reports since 1967, 58 of them golf-ball size or larger, and the county’s largest stone, <a href="https://www.ncdc.noaa.gov/stormevents/eventdetails.jsp?id=5135628" target="_blank" rel="noopener">4.5 inches, fell just north of San Marcos on March 16, 2000</a>. On May 9, 2024, <a href="https://www.ncdc.noaa.gov/stormevents/eventdetails.jsp?id=1181388" target="_blank" rel="noopener">3-inch hail fell at San Marcos Academy</a> and 70 mph gusts damaged roofs and downed trees across the city.</p>
<p>Water is the other big risk. San Marcos sits on the Balcones Escarpment in “Flash Flood Alley,” and during the Memorial Day flood of May 2015 the San Marcos River crested at 43.08 feet while the NWS issued a Flash Flood Emergency for the city. New FEMA flood maps took effect January 17, 2025. Housing ranges from newer slab-on-grade subdivisions with composition shingle roofs, to student rentals and apartment complexes near Texas State, to older homes in the historic neighborhoods near downtown, plus flat and low-slope commercial roofs along I-35. Repairs inside city limits follow the city’s adopted codes; see our <a href="/local-building-codes/">San Marcos building codes guide</a>.</p>

