<h3><a href="/service-areas/kyle/">Kyle</a></h3>
<p>A growing Hays County city on I-35 with many newer subdivisions. NOAA records <a href="https://www.ncdc.noaa.gov/stormevents/eventdetails.jsp?id=869349" target="_blank" rel="noopener">75 mph gusts on January 10, 2020</a> that blew siding off a house and left multiple homes with shingle damage, and <a href="https://www.ncdc.noaa.gov/stormevents/eventdetails.jsp?id=1264431" target="_blank" rel="noopener">tennis-ball-size hail near Simon Middle School on May 22, 2025</a>.</p>

<h3><a href="/service-areas/buda/">Buda</a></h3>
<p>At the north end of Hays County near the Travis County line. During the October 30–31, 2015 storms, an observer just west-northwest of Buda measured 18.46 inches of rain in two days, part of the flooding covered by <a href="https://www.fema.gov/disaster/4245" target="_blank" rel="noopener">FEMA DR-4245</a>.</p>

<h3><a href="/service-areas/wimberley/">Wimberley</a></h3>
<p>A Hill Country community on the Blanco River and Cypress Creek. In the May 2015 Memorial Day flood the Blanco River at Wimberley rose from about 5 feet to about 41 feet in roughly four hours (<a href="https://www.fema.gov/disaster/4223" target="_blank" rel="noopener">FEMA DR-4223</a>). NOAA also lists an <a href="https://www.ncdc.noaa.gov/stormevents/eventdetails.jsp?id=674534" target="_blank" rel="noopener">EF1 tornado on February 19, 2017</a> and two EF0 tornadoes south of town on June 12, 2025.</p>

<h3><a href="/service-areas/dripping-springs/">Dripping Springs</a></h3>
<p>In northwest Hays County along US 290. NOAA records <a href="https://www.ncdc.noaa.gov/stormevents/eventdetails.jsp?id=1181349" target="_blank" rel="noopener">3-inch hail south of Dripping Springs on May 9, 2024</a>, and the January–February 2023 ice storm left about half an inch of ice there.</p>

<h3><a href="/service-areas/new-braunfels/">New Braunfels</a></h3>
<p>Mostly in Comal County, with part of the city in Guadalupe County, along I-35 southwest of San Marcos. It is home to the National Weather Service Austin/San Antonio office that issues forecasts and warnings for the whole area. New Braunfels has its own permit office and code adoptions.</p>

<h3><a href="/service-areas/lockhart/">Lockhart</a></h3>
<p>The Caldwell County seat, east of San Marcos. Lockhart properties fall outside the Hays County storm record on this site, so search the NOAA database by Caldwell County for local events.</p>

<h3><a href="/service-areas/seguin/">Seguin</a></h3>
<p>The Guadalupe County seat on the Guadalupe River, south of San Marcos. The October 1998 flood washed homes off their foundations along the Guadalupe from Canyon Lake to Seguin, according to the National Weather Service.</p>

<h3><a href="/service-areas/martindale/">Martindale</a></h3>
<p>A small Caldwell County city on the San Marcos River just downstream of San Marcos. During the October 2013 Halloween flood, the NWS noted the San Marcos River flooding near Martindale.</p>

<h3>Other nearby communities</h3>
<p>We also work with property owners in <strong>Maxwell</strong> (unincorporated Caldwell County), <strong>Uhland</strong> (split between Hays and Caldwell counties), <strong>Niederwald</strong>, <strong>Driftwood</strong>, and <strong>Redwood</strong>. These smaller places have their own entries in the storm record: <a href="https://www.ncdc.noaa.gov/stormevents/eventdetails.jsp?id=1264433" target="_blank" rel="noopener">baseball-size hail in Uhland on May 22, 2025</a>, an <a href="https://www.ncdc.noaa.gov/stormevents/eventdetails.jsp?id=835459" target="_blank" rel="noopener">80 mph gust that blew a large section of roof off a house in Niederwald</a> on June 9, 2019, 12 to 14 inches of rain from Wimberley to Driftwood in the October 2013 flood, and high water and a water rescue around Redwood in late May 2015.</p>

